# Engine: Claude Code — FREE-tier overlay
# v10.16 — sourced by start_agents_tmux.sh AFTER claude.env when the
# user passes --free.
#
# ============================================================================
# NOTE — Claude has no "truly free" tier
# ============================================================================
# Anthropic does not offer a $0 API model. What --free means for Claude:
#
#   1. Force every role to claude-haiku-4-5 (the cheapest tier — roughly
#      ~$1 per million input / ~$5 per million output).
#   2. If you are on a Pro/Max subscription (no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY set),
#      ALL Claude usage counts against your monthly quota, not metered.
#      In that case haiku is "effectively free" — just minimizes quota
#      burn so you can re-run workflows many times.
#
# If you have ANTHROPIC_API_KEY set, start_agents_tmux.sh will refuse to
# launch unless CLAUDE_API_MODE_ACK=1. Even with --free, you'd be paying
# (just less than the default sonnet/opus mix).
# ============================================================================

# All 9 roles → claude-haiku-4-5. Workflow correctness still tests
# correctly because the framework's protocols (routing, watch, etc.)
# don't depend on which Claude tier runs them.
ORCHESTRATOR_MODEL="claude-haiku-4-5"
PM_MODEL="claude-haiku-4-5"
SA_MODEL="claude-haiku-4-5"
BA_MODEL="claude-haiku-4-5"
UX_MODEL="claude-haiku-4-5"
BE_MODEL="claude-haiku-4-5"
FE_MODEL="claude-haiku-4-5"
QA_MODEL="claude-haiku-4-5"
DELIVERY_MODEL="claude-haiku-4-5"
